# Shell scripts must keep LF endings whatever the platform they are cloned
# on. A CRLF checkout turns the shebang into `#!/bin/sh\r`, which Linux
# cannot resolve: the container then dies with "not found" on a file that is
# plainly there, and the whole backend crash-loops. Cloning on Windows with
# core.autocrlf=true is enough to trigger it.
*.sh text eol=lf

# The same applies to anything a container executes or parses directly.
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.Dockerfile text eol=lf
docker-compose.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
